WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:03.890
The inter-school tournament is heating up!

00:03.890 --> 00:06.650
After trailing by a goal, Nankatsu

00:06.650 --> 00:09.440
was saved when Ishizaki sacrificed himself,

00:09.440 --> 00:14.740
allowing Tsubasa to score with a game-tying overhead kick.

00:15.610 --> 00:18.620
Wakabayashi felt the pain of defeat upon surrendering a goal,

00:19.740 --> 00:24.960
but his teammates' feelings managed to rouse him back to his feet.

00:24.960 --> 00:26.210
Who the hell are you?

00:26.670 --> 00:28.960
I'm Taro Misaki.

00:28.960 --> 00:30.670
I look forward to playing with you, Tsubasa!

00:31.920 --> 00:36.180
Tsubasa and the team had Taro Misaki replace the injured Ishizaki

00:36.180 --> 00:39.390
allowing them to control the pace of the match.

00:39.390 --> 00:41.060
But, in the second half of extra time, with

00:41.060 --> 00:46.150
Taki's corner kick, Wakabayashi struck with a powerful shot.

00:46.810 --> 00:48.440
Wakabayashi wasn't satisfied, declaring their aim to score again

00:48.440 --> 00:51.570
to ensure their victory, but

00:52.230 --> 00:54.450
Tsubasa has yet to accept defeat.

00:54.450 --> 00:56.160
Aiming for victory,

00:56.160 --> 01:00.080
both he and Misaki's spirits are running high!

01:12.090 --> 01:17.720
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:12.090 --> 01:17.720
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:17.720 --> 01:22.720
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:17.720 --> 01:22.720
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:23.390 --> 01:28.560
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:23.390 --> 01:28.560
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:29.270 --> 01:36.900
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:29.270 --> 01:36.900
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:36.900 --> 01:42.660
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:36.900 --> 01:42.660
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:42.660 --> 01:51.170
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:42.660 --> 01:51.170
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:51.170 --> 01:56.970
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:51.170 --> 01:56.970
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:56.970 --> 02:02.890
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:56.970 --> 02:02.890
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

02:02.890 --> 02:04.390
<i>Run & Run!</i>

02:04.390 --> 02:11.690
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

02:04.390 --> 02:11.690
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:11.690 --> 02:14.610
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

02:11.690 --> 02:14.610
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

02:14.610 --> 02:19.530
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

02:14.610 --> 02:19.530
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:30.290 --> 02:34.210
<b><b>EPISODE 9:
A HAPPY ENDING</b></b>

02:38.010 --> 02:39.630
We are a minute into the second half of extra time,

02:39.630 --> 02:41.590
and with keeper Wakabayashi's goal,

02:41.590 --> 02:44.310
Shutetsu is in the lead again!

02:44.310 --> 02:48.350
Nankatsu has to make up ground once more!

02:48.350 --> 02:50.270
We'll catch up for sure!

02:50.270 --> 02:52.060
Yeah!

02:52.060 --> 02:55.070
That's right! The match isn't over yet!

02:55.070 --> 02:58.190
<i>My legs will give everything they've got to make it tied! </i>

02:59.490 --> 03:02.870
You have nothing to worry about anymore, Genzo.

03:03.950 --> 03:05.620
The match resumes!

03:05.620 --> 03:09.160
As it is an inter-school match, there is no more extra time.

03:09.160 --> 03:12.630
Can Nankatsu possibly tie or overcome them

03:12.630 --> 03:14.790
with just four minutes of time remaining?

03:14.790 --> 03:17.670
Don't let them regain their pace, get the ball back!

03:17.670 --> 03:20.130
Tsubasa can tie this up for sure!

03:20.130 --> 03:21.680
Tsubasa!

03:21.680 --> 03:23.220
Go, take your shot!

03:23.220 --> 03:25.140
Misaki!

03:28.060 --> 03:32.600
With all the chances these two have created, expectations are still high!

03:32.600 --> 03:33.980
Shimada, get to Tsubasa!

03:33.980 --> 03:35.480
Nakamoto, get to Misaki!

03:35.480 --> 03:36.860
Mark both of them thoroughly!

03:36.860 --> 03:38.110
Yes, captain!

03:38.860 --> 03:39.940
All right!

03:41.900 --> 03:45.830
Whoa! Tsubasa sends a long pass to the flank!

03:45.830 --> 03:46.830
Got it!

03:47.540 --> 03:50.910
Nankatsu's passes are connecting, and the team pushes forward on the attack!

03:50.910 --> 03:53.370
That's it, everyone! That's the way!

03:55.130 --> 03:57.040
Iwami is quickly approaching the goal!

03:57.250 --> 04:00.550
<i>Sure, but we all know the shooter will be either Tsubasa or Misaki...!</i>

04:01.050 --> 04:03.970
Both Tsubasa and Misaki are approaching from either side!

04:03.970 --> 04:05.090
Here they come!

04:05.090 --> 04:07.350
Shutetsu's defenders try to intervene!

04:08.470 --> 04:10.100
Counting on you!

04:10.100 --> 04:12.850
Iwami dodges and crosses the ball in!

04:12.850 --> 04:15.600
Who is it for, Tsubasa or Misaki?

04:20.070 --> 04:22.700
Wakabayashi intercepts it with a leaping catch!

04:24.450 --> 04:26.070
Good move, Genzo.

04:26.070 --> 04:28.950
You can keep this up for rest of the match.

04:28.950 --> 04:31.160
This time, Wakabayashi makes a nice save!

04:31.160 --> 04:32.250
Go!

04:32.250 --> 04:33.580
Everyone, fall back!

04:35.460 --> 04:37.790
Nankatsu's players quickly pull back to defend!

04:37.790 --> 04:42.800
It's so late into extra time, and they don't look winded at all!

04:42.800 --> 04:45.590
Where were they hiding all this energy?

04:45.590 --> 04:48.390
Oh hell, they're going to try the birdcage again!

04:48.390 --> 04:49.600
What? Birdcage?!

04:51.020 --> 04:53.020
We're not interested in that, anymore!

04:53.020 --> 04:54.270
We'll aiming to score!

04:54.270 --> 04:55.850
We'll secure our victory!

04:55.850 --> 04:56.690
That's right!

04:56.690 --> 04:58.860
Show them the dignity of Shutetsu!

04:58.860 --> 04:59.900
Kisugi!

05:00.480 --> 05:03.400
And now the ball is sent up to Shutetsu's lead scorer!

05:03.400 --> 05:06.410
Will Shutetsu be able to score the decisive third goal?!

05:06.410 --> 05:07.660
Like I'd let you!

05:09.160 --> 05:11.540
Wait, he passed to the right instead of shooting?!

05:11.540 --> 05:14.330
Izawa is making a run for it!

05:15.830 --> 05:18.130
The keeper stretches, but can't react...!

05:19.380 --> 05:20.340
Misaki!

05:20.340 --> 05:21.170
Misaki blocks it!

05:21.170 --> 05:23.170
Misaki has shown us a fine play!

05:23.170 --> 05:24.670
That's great, Misaki!

05:26.050 --> 05:28.470
That guy, when did he...?

05:28.470 --> 05:30.390
It's our turn to attack now!

05:30.390 --> 05:31.510
All of you, stop him!

05:35.230 --> 05:39.650
Misaki dribbles ahead, reminiscent of Tsubasa's earlier moves!

05:39.650 --> 05:41.190
I'll even the score!

05:41.190 --> 05:42.230
You won't get past me!

05:43.480 --> 05:45.030
He gets by with ease!

05:45.030 --> 05:47.110
Being that he was such a late substitution,

05:47.110 --> 05:48.110
he is full of energy!

05:48.110 --> 05:50.320
His dribbling is so sharp!

05:50.320 --> 05:52.620
It's no wonder we were no match for him...

05:54.620 --> 05:58.370
That Taro. I thought he was late. So this is what he's up to?

05:58.830 --> 06:00.790
Less than three minutes remain!

06:00.790 --> 06:04.630
Nankatsu needs to make use of this chance!

06:06.090 --> 06:07.550
He dodges another player!

06:07.550 --> 06:09.550
Misaki leaves everyone in the dust as he speeds ahead!

06:09.550 --> 06:12.560
But here is Tsubasa, approaching from the other side!

06:12.850 --> 06:13.640
Come!

06:13.640 --> 06:15.430
Go for it, Nankatsu!

06:15.890 --> 06:18.940
Genzo, this is your last trial.

06:18.940 --> 06:21.400
I'm counting on you... Tsubasa, Misaki!

06:21.400 --> 06:24.400
Wakabayashi stands firm as his challengers approach!

06:24.400 --> 06:28.400
Will Tsubasa shoot? Or will it be Misaki?

06:28.780 --> 06:29.700
Stop him!

06:29.700 --> 06:31.740
Shutetsu's defense comes up!

06:31.740 --> 06:32.780
Tsubasa!

06:32.780 --> 06:36.000
Misaki crosses the ball into an opening!

06:36.000 --> 06:38.660
So it's you in the end, huh, Tsubasa?!

06:39.580 --> 06:40.790
What?!

06:40.790 --> 06:43.960
Tsubasa foregoes the shot and passes the ball back!

06:43.960 --> 06:46.550
Misaki comes in with a diving header!

06:47.170 --> 06:48.970
I won't let you!

06:48.970 --> 06:50.550
Wakabayashi's reaction is relentless!

06:51.930 --> 06:54.180
Wait, Misaki passes it back again!

07:01.400 --> 07:03.480
They scored, GOAL!

07:05.110 --> 07:07.110
The game is tied!

07:07.110 --> 07:10.570
Nankatsu has tied the score again!

07:10.570 --> 07:12.110
We did it!

07:13.030 --> 07:14.120
Tsubasa!

07:14.120 --> 07:16.290
We did it! Yay!

07:16.290 --> 07:18.120
Tsubasa, nice shot!

07:18.120 --> 07:20.540
Nice assist, Misaki!

07:20.540 --> 07:24.710
What a wonderful double play from Tsubasa and Misaki!

07:24.710 --> 07:26.710
You're so cool, Tsubasa!

07:26.710 --> 07:28.260
You did good, Tsubasa!

07:28.260 --> 07:29.470
It's a tie!

07:29.470 --> 07:31.260
We did it, coach!

07:31.260 --> 07:31.930
Yes.

07:31.930 --> 07:34.430
You did it, Tsubasa!

07:37.930 --> 07:39.020
Taro...

07:44.560 --> 07:47.940
Genzo, this one was unavoidable.

07:50.950 --> 07:52.530
Captain...

07:52.530 --> 07:54.780
Captain, we're sorry.

07:54.780 --> 07:58.080
We didn't mark them...

07:58.080 --> 07:59.580
What's gotten into you guys?

08:00.790 --> 08:03.370
They haven't out-scored us yet.

08:03.370 --> 08:04.790
Get back at them!

08:04.790 --> 08:05.920
Captain!

08:05.920 --> 08:07.880
We still have time!

08:07.880 --> 08:09.090
Let's give it our all!

08:09.090 --> 08:10.460
Yes, captain!

08:11.340 --> 08:13.970
It's like a game of cat and mouse!

08:13.970 --> 08:18.560
We can't guess how this game will end!
There are only 2 minutes left in this match!

08:18.970 --> 08:22.270
We'll win for sure! For our captain as well!

08:24.770 --> 08:25.690
Let's go!

08:25.690 --> 08:26.650
Yeah!

08:26.650 --> 08:29.860
The match resumes, and the heated clash continues!

08:29.860 --> 08:31.650
Shutetsu attacks!

08:31.650 --> 08:33.700
But Nankatsu has stolen the ball!

08:34.160 --> 08:35.990
Shutetsu wins it back!

08:36.620 --> 08:39.240
Both teams have played for over 45 minutes.

08:39.240 --> 08:41.450
They are tired to their roots, but

08:41.450 --> 08:45.040
they are still aiming for victory, playing through their exhaustion!

08:45.040 --> 08:47.920
There's less than a minute left in the match!

08:47.920 --> 08:51.090
There will be no more extra time after this!

08:51.090 --> 08:52.970
Fight, Nankatsu!

08:52.970 --> 08:54.970
Don't lose, Shutetsu!

08:54.970 --> 08:56.800
A cross for Kisugi goes up!

08:58.100 --> 09:01.310
Nankatsu defenders put pressure on him!

09:01.310 --> 09:02.140
Damn it!

09:02.560 --> 09:03.770
He shoots from below!

09:04.230 --> 09:07.020
Straight to the keeper!

09:07.310 --> 09:08.980
Recovers the ball and makes a long pass to open space!

09:10.440 --> 09:12.400
Takasugi! Go, mark him!

09:12.820 --> 09:14.860
Takasugi with a sliding tackle!

09:14.860 --> 09:16.450
Alright, time to attack!

09:17.160 --> 09:19.240
Misaki steals the ball!

09:19.240 --> 09:22.240
There are only moments left in this game!

09:22.620 --> 09:23.750
Tsubasa!

09:24.870 --> 09:25.710
Alright!

09:26.120 --> 09:27.580
The referee is looking at his watch!

09:27.580 --> 09:29.590
Leave it to me!

09:30.800 --> 09:34.670
Wakabayashi and Tsubasa move towards the ball!

09:34.670 --> 09:36.340
Tsubasa!

09:38.680 --> 09:39.850
Captain!

09:40.720 --> 09:44.350
Wakabayashi and Tsubasa jump up simultaneously!

09:44.350 --> 09:48.020
This is their last bout!

10:09.080 --> 10:11.340
No goal!

10:13.000 --> 10:17.510
That's it! The sign to end the match!

10:17.510 --> 10:23.100
After 50 minutes of playtime, the football match

10:23.100 --> 10:26.600
ends without a decisive goal! It's a tie!

10:26.600 --> 10:30.350
The 26th inter-school tournament

10:30.350 --> 10:33.650
has ended in a draw, for only the second time in its history!

10:41.490 --> 10:43.580
You got me, Tsubasa.

10:43.580 --> 10:45.040
It's a tie, then.

10:46.370 --> 10:47.710
Tsubasa!

10:48.210 --> 10:49.710
Genzo!

10:54.210 --> 10:56.590
It's over!

10:56.590 --> 11:01.260
As soon as I thought about the game being over, I'm suddenly aching all over...

11:01.260 --> 11:02.850
Me too!

11:02.850 --> 11:05.640
I've kinda lost all the power in my body.

11:05.640 --> 11:08.310
Nice match, Nankatsu!

11:08.810 --> 11:11.480
We didn't think you would play this well.

11:11.480 --> 11:13.440
I've changed my opinion about you guys.

11:14.980 --> 11:17.570
You all did well!

11:17.570 --> 11:20.200
That's Shutetsu, Japan's best for you!

11:20.200 --> 11:21.820
You did well too, Nankatsu!

11:21.820 --> 11:26.580
Nobody will ever call you a lame football club again!

11:30.370 --> 11:35.420
Tsubasa, let's meet on the pitch again.

11:35.420 --> 11:36.500
Yes!

11:42.430 --> 11:44.140
Thank you for cheering today!

11:47.060 --> 11:48.720
Tsubasa!

11:50.390 --> 11:52.690
Boss!

11:53.190 --> 11:56.610
Tsubasa, it was a nice game.

11:56.610 --> 11:57.570
Yeah.

11:59.150 --> 12:01.070
But, this is just the beginning.

12:01.070 --> 12:06.030
Your life as a footballer has only just begun!

12:31.390 --> 12:33.140
Good morning, Roberto.

12:33.140 --> 12:34.600
Good morning!

12:36.020 --> 12:37.770
Huh, where is Tsubasa?

12:37.770 --> 12:40.780
Isn't it obvious? Gone to play football again.

12:40.780 --> 12:44.450
The inter-school tournament just ended, and yet...

12:44.450 --> 12:45.780
That boy...

12:50.290 --> 12:51.450
All right!

12:51.450 --> 12:53.040
Not there yet!

12:53.040 --> 12:55.710
I can't believe they can still keep at this.

12:55.710 --> 12:56.830
You said it.

12:56.830 --> 13:00.550
I'm exhausted from all the work from the inter-school tournament.

13:01.130 --> 13:04.050
I wonder which one of them is better?

13:05.180 --> 13:06.970
Their skill at dribbling is about equal, but...

13:06.970 --> 13:09.640
I guess Tsubasa is better when it comes to shooting.

13:09.640 --> 13:11.060
Yeah, you're right.

13:11.060 --> 13:13.730
Now, here comes a shot from Taro Misaki, from Nankatsu Elementary!

13:17.060 --> 13:19.730
Can you still say that after seeing this?

13:19.730 --> 13:22.740
Anyway, as long as we have both of them,

13:22.740 --> 13:24.780
the national tournament isn't a distant dream!

13:24.780 --> 13:28.240
Yeah! Let's beat Shutetsu in the next inter-prefecture tournament

13:28.240 --> 13:29.780
and attend to the Nationals!

13:29.780 --> 13:31.540
That's going to be impossible.

13:32.790 --> 13:34.660
Ishizaki!

13:34.660 --> 13:35.460
Hi!

13:35.460 --> 13:37.080
Why is it impossible?!

13:36.440 --> 13:38.140
Oh, it's Ishizaki!

13:37.080 --> 13:39.540
Yeah! We tied them in the inter-school tournament after all!

13:39.540 --> 13:43.590
I'm not saying we can't beat Shutetsu,

13:43.590 --> 13:48.300
but Nankatsu City decided to create a local team selection.

13:48.300 --> 13:49.930
Local team selection?

13:49.930 --> 13:50.930
What are you talking about?

13:50.930 --> 13:52.390
Hey there, Tsubasa!

13:52.890 --> 13:54.520
Well, until now, schools have participated in

13:54.520 --> 13:57.520
prefecture preliminaries on their own, separately.

13:57.520 --> 14:01.980
This year, Nankatsu City has decided to gather the best from each school,

14:01.980 --> 14:05.360
and create the Nankatsu Youth Football Club to represent the city.

14:05.360 --> 14:07.780
The level in the national tournament is increasing as well,

14:07.780 --> 14:12.120
so most of the other cities are forming their own city clubs.

14:12.120 --> 14:16.040
You mean we might play alongside members from Shutetsu?

14:16.040 --> 14:18.790
Yeah. If you want to participate in the Nationals,

14:18.790 --> 14:21.790
you'll have to make it into the city selection first.

14:21.790 --> 14:24.050
Apparently, there are going to be tryouts soon.

14:24.050 --> 14:25.380
Tryouts, huh?

14:25.380 --> 14:28.720
All right! I've got to work hard to pass too!

14:28.720 --> 14:31.010
There is no way they'll pick you, Manabu.

14:31.010 --> 14:32.260
You won't be able to make it in, even as a substitute!

14:32.260 --> 14:33.680
That's not true!

14:33.680 --> 14:35.640
We tied against Shutetsu.

14:35.640 --> 14:36.600
Even I can do it!

14:36.600 --> 14:39.230
Yeah, if we practice hard enough, it'll work out, somehow!

14:39.230 --> 14:43.070
All right! Let's start our training for the tryouts!

14:43.070 --> 14:44.650
Yeah!

14:46.150 --> 14:50.200
They've gained a lot of confidence since the inter-school tournament.

14:50.200 --> 14:51.530
That goes for me too, though.

14:52.620 --> 14:55.490
So, what are you planning to do, Roberto?

14:55.490 --> 14:58.790
Well, I'm thinking of going back to Brazil.

14:58.790 --> 15:00.370
Is that so?

15:00.370 --> 15:01.500
What are you going to do after that?

15:01.500 --> 15:04.340
You don't need to worry about me, Captain.

15:04.340 --> 15:06.590
That won't be happening again.

15:06.590 --> 15:07.920
What do you mean by <i>that</i>?

15:07.920 --> 15:09.720
Well, actually...

15:10.380 --> 15:13.470
That incident was also how I met with the Captain.

15:16.180 --> 15:22.810
I'm ashamed to say it, but I was living as an aimless drunkard, miserable and depressed

15:22.810 --> 15:25.900
ever since the doctor told me I should give up football.

15:29.030 --> 15:32.910
Well, if I couldn't play the football which I had bet my entire life on,

15:32.910 --> 15:34.580
I figured, well, I would die sooner or later. So...

15:36.120 --> 15:39.460
Whoa, a person just jumped!

15:39.460 --> 15:40.460
What?!

15:40.460 --> 15:41.120
That's insane!

15:41.120 --> 15:42.580
How could they do that?!

15:43.830 --> 15:46.590
Captain saved me on the spot.

15:46.590 --> 15:51.880
Not only that, but he also introduced me to the world's best ophthalmologist.

15:51.880 --> 15:54.260
It's unfortunate how the results turned out, though.

15:54.260 --> 15:58.720
You felt so cornered, especially since you really dedicated your entirely life to football.

15:58.720 --> 16:00.850
Well, not as much as Tsubasa.

16:03.060 --> 16:07.860
You know, this may sound unreasonable coming from a troublemaker like me, but...

16:07.860 --> 16:10.990
I have one more request from you.

16:10.990 --> 16:13.030
Request?

16:16.450 --> 16:17.790
Well done, Genzo!

16:17.790 --> 16:19.330
That's it for today.

16:19.330 --> 16:21.830
Mr. Mikami, I can keep going.

16:21.830 --> 16:24.830
Tsubasa and his friends must still be practicing.

16:24.830 --> 16:28.340
You still haven't recovered from the inter-school tournament.

16:28.340 --> 16:30.170
It's not good to overexert yourself.

16:30.170 --> 16:31.380
Yes, sir.

16:31.800 --> 16:35.220
Young Master! Young Master!

16:35.220 --> 16:38.260
There's a shipment for you!

16:44.020 --> 16:47.690
Is there something interesting in the magazine, Genzo?

16:47.690 --> 16:50.570
I am going out for a bit, Mr. Mikami.

16:50.570 --> 16:51.780
All right, I'm starting.

16:51.780 --> 16:52.990
Keep yourself together!

16:52.990 --> 16:54.700
He went that way!

16:54.700 --> 16:56.070
Damn it!

16:56.070 --> 16:59.450
Argh, I wanna practice too.

16:59.450 --> 17:02.200
Won't it get better already?

17:02.200 --> 17:03.750
Ouch!

17:05.370 --> 17:06.000
Huh?

17:07.420 --> 17:09.000
Oh, Wakabayashi!

17:09.420 --> 17:12.260
You know, I thought I'd get to try and beat you this time,

17:12.260 --> 17:14.510
but now they're saying they'll be selecting a team for the city.

17:14.510 --> 17:16.010
Sure is unnecessary...

17:16.010 --> 17:18.600
Forget about that — tell me where Roberto Hongo is!

17:18.600 --> 17:21.100
That's a threatening look in your eyes...

17:21.100 --> 17:23.140
Coach hasn't been here today.

17:23.140 --> 17:26.400
Did you know about his eyes?

17:26.400 --> 17:27.150
Huh?

17:27.150 --> 17:29.110
What are you talking about?

17:29.110 --> 17:30.980
So you really don't know?!

17:32.610 --> 17:35.820
Roberto Hongo can't play football anymore!

17:35.820 --> 17:36.740
What?

17:36.740 --> 17:38.240
Roberto is...

17:38.240 --> 17:40.120
Look at this.

17:41.370 --> 17:43.370
Retirement?!

17:43.370 --> 17:45.460
Wait, why did our coach retire?

17:45.460 --> 17:47.420
He was diagnosed with retinal detachment.

17:47.420 --> 17:49.500
But he can play together with us!

17:49.500 --> 17:52.420
Don't mix the professional stage with our elementary school football!

17:52.420 --> 17:57.390
He may be able to play with you, but he can no longer stand in the same field with the pros!

17:57.930 --> 17:59.890
Roberto...

18:00.680 --> 18:01.890
Tsubasa!

18:02.220 --> 18:04.390
I will ask Roberto directly!

18:06.600 --> 18:09.560
Okay then, we're coming, too!

18:12.070 --> 18:13.820
Roberto is retiring?

18:14.690 --> 18:18.320
Be friends with the ball.

18:18.320 --> 18:21.080
Not being able to play...!

18:21.080 --> 18:23.240
What?

18:23.240 --> 18:25.160
I am begging you, Captain!

18:25.160 --> 18:26.660
Also you too, Mrs. Ozora!

18:26.660 --> 18:31.840
I will definitely make him grow into a world-class player!

18:31.840 --> 18:32.460
So please...

18:32.840 --> 18:33.500
Roberto!

18:33.500 --> 18:36.760
Please, let me take Tsubasa to Brazil!

18:39.010 --> 18:40.220
Tsubasa!

18:41.600 --> 18:47.140
Roberto... is it true that you can't play football anymore?

18:47.140 --> 18:48.390
Yeah.

18:48.390 --> 18:50.770
You really can't play football?

18:50.770 --> 18:52.150
Yeah.

18:52.150 --> 18:55.530
I can never stand on the football pitch again.

19:00.410 --> 19:04.410
Roberto, Brazil is a football country, right?

19:05.290 --> 19:06.580
It sure is!

19:06.580 --> 19:11.170
All of its citizens love football, and live their lives with it.

19:12.080 --> 19:15.550
Roberto, I am coming with you to Brazil!

19:16.920 --> 19:18.170
Tsubasa...

19:19.590 --> 19:23.680
Then, we'll have to play to our heart's content until then.

19:25.560 --> 19:30.900
Okay, guys! We're giving these tryouts our best!

19:30.900 --> 19:33.940
We'll pass them and play together with Tsubasa in the Nationals!

19:33.940 --> 19:35.570
Yeah!

19:42.160 --> 19:47.330
The day for the Nankatsu Youth tryouts has arrived!

19:48.410 --> 19:52.120
The tryouts are held in a match format.

19:52.120 --> 19:57.420
Coach Shiroyama and his staff watch each of them for 5 minutes and make evaluations.

19:58.920 --> 20:06.810
The team was built around Wakabayashi, and the Shutetsu Quartet has demonstrated their skills.

20:06.810 --> 20:11.480
At this rate, we might select everyone from Shutetsu.

20:11.480 --> 20:13.400
Don't be so sure, yet.

20:13.400 --> 20:15.610
There are many players here.

20:15.610 --> 20:18.820
There ought to be some players that are better than Shutetsu's!

20:21.820 --> 20:22.610
Tsubasa!

20:30.710 --> 20:32.330
That was a jumping volley!

20:32.330 --> 20:34.330
That's way beyond an elementary school level!

20:34.330 --> 20:36.090
Shit, it is going to be Tsubasa after all.

20:36.090 --> 20:37.420
Terrific!

20:37.420 --> 20:40.050
I've decided on the the center-forward for our team.

20:40.050 --> 20:41.630
Roberto!

20:41.630 --> 20:45.640
I'll win the National Tournament and go to Brazil together after that.

20:46.100 --> 20:47.970
Tsubasa...

20:48.350 --> 20:49.350
Young ones!

20:49.350 --> 20:52.770
You all did well in the heat today.

20:52.770 --> 20:55.480
Your vigorous plays are sure to be seen by the coa–

20:55.480 --> 20:58.650
Get on with it and just announce the selected players!

20:58.650 --> 21:00.150
Yeah, he's right!

21:00.150 --> 21:02.150
But... I'm the mayor...

21:02.820 --> 21:04.410
Here are the results of the tryout!

21:04.410 --> 21:09.240
From Shutetsu, Wakabayashi and the Shutetsu Quartet.

21:09.240 --> 21:13.500
From Nishigaoka, Urabe. From Yamabuki, Kishida.

21:13.500 --> 21:19.170
From Nankatsu, Tsubasa, Misaki and Ishizaki.

21:19.800 --> 21:22.340
Looks like I managed to make it in!

21:22.340 --> 21:25.890
Tsubasa, it looks like we're part of the same team this time.

21:25.890 --> 21:26.840
I'm looking forward to it!

21:26.840 --> 21:28.720
Yeah.

21:28.720 --> 21:32.100
50, 51, 52, 53...

21:36.270 --> 21:38.400
It'll be fine to let Roberto look after Tsubasa.

21:40.440 --> 21:44.070
It'll be better for Tsubasa's growth as a player to be in Brazil.

21:44.070 --> 21:45.650
We might get a little lonely,

21:45.650 --> 21:48.490
but parents shouldn't get in the way of children pursuing their dreams.

21:50.160 --> 21:51.370
You're right.

21:51.370 --> 21:56.330
For Tsubasa, instead of being confined to Japan, the vast lands of Brazil will suit him better.

21:56.330 --> 22:00.250
Yeah. Don't lose to yourself, Tsubasa!

22:00.250 --> 22:02.670
99, 100!

22:02.670 --> 22:04.670
Roberto, I did a hundred!

22:04.670 --> 22:08.760
Okay! Now, lift the ball 200 times while using your head and knees.

22:08.760 --> 22:09.890
Sure!

22:11.430 --> 22:14.730
1, 2, 3, 4...

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.730
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.730
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.730 --> 23:02.190
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.730 --> 23:02.190
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:08.320
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:08.320
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.040
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.040
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.040 --> 23:21.080
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.380 --> 23:33.260
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.380 --> 23:33.260
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.260 --> 23:39.140
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:46.030
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:46.030
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.110 --> 24:00.460
COMING UP, EPISODE 10 :
KOJIRO ARRIVES
